KZ2 patch 2182: a background pipeline build and its walker retry never build the
same entry at once.

Written for the Pyrrhus native Mac bring-up; no game code or RPCS3 code used.
Licence: MIT (project LICENSE).

The worker of patch 2179 read "not being built inline" under the build lock,
let the lock go and started compiling without saying so. A re-request from the
walker more than 5 s after the insert saw neither flag, marked itself the
builder and compiled the same entry. When the worker finished first it freed
the two HLSL texts while the walker was still translating them: the walker's
build failed on a garbage string ("HLSL parse: ERROR: 0:1: '<bad token>'") and
then stored 0 over the worker's good result. From then on every draw with that
pipeline was dropped, for the rest of the session -- ten entries in one
cruiser run, scene parts missing.

The worker now claims the entry (worker_building) in the same locked section in
which it checks for an inline build, and a retry only builds inline an entry no
worker has claimed; otherwise it returns 0 for this draw and the worker's
result serves the next one.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
index ddd28dd..f9725a2 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
@@ -3212,6 +3212,7 @@ static int eng_stage_copy(const void* src, u32 bytes, u32* out_off)
     u32 result;                 /* 0 while in flight, the handle once done */
     int done;
     int inline_building;        /* a retry built it on the walker; the worker skips */
+    int worker_building;        /* patch 2182: the worker took it; a retry waits for its result */
     uint64_t queued_us;         /* ps3_ft_now() at insert, for the retry age gate */
     char* vs_hlsl;              /* the worker's own copies; freed on its way out */
     char* ps_hlsl;
@@ -3747,14 +3748,18 @@ static void eng_async_insert(u64 key, const char* vs_hlsl, const char* ps_hlsl,
             pthread_mutex_lock(&s_eng_build_lock);
             const int done = b->done;
             const int inline_bld = b->inline_building;
-            pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_eng_build_lock);
             if (done) {
+                pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_eng_build_lock);
                 free(b->vs_hlsl); b->vs_hlsl = NULL;
                 free(b->ps_hlsl); b->ps_hlsl = NULL;
                 dispatch_semaphore_signal(s_eng_build_slots);
                 return;
